  "change": [
    "Replace general HIP pitched copies of large recurrent-state groups with an exact uint4 copy, 256x1 threads per workgroup. The prior HIP copy uses 16x16; the new workgroup covers contiguous columns of one row group.",
    "The arena selects this route for layer rows >= 1 MiB, 16-byte aligned pitches and a complete live group span <=UINT32_MAX bytes. Other layouts retain HIP. Tail groups keep their existing contiguous copy.",
    "Live/saved layouts, copied bytes, allocations, convolution snapshots, stream synchronization and replay semantics are unchanged. No model arithmetic, draft, sampler, controller or execution option changes.",
    "The existing rollback fixture checks both small and 48x128x128 recurrent states in FP32/BF16. Six layer/attention-interval combinations, both sizes and both storage types run two saves/restores each: 48 cycles. Every recurrent byte must be restored; skipped attention rows must retain the poison byte."
  ],
